<title>GERMANY: Welteke calls for debt recalculation in Euro.</title>
<headline>Welteke calls for debt recalculation in Euro.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bundesbank council member Ernst Welteke urged on Monday a speedy recalculation of German government debt into the new Euro once currency union is launched.</p>
<p>&quot;So that we do not have split markets, I urge a speedy switchover of bonds into the new Euro currency,&quot; Welteke said in answering a question after a speech to foreign bankers in Frankfurt.</p>
<p>He said a quick recaculation of already-issued bonds is necessary so that market interest in the debt does not dry up.</p>
<p>The Bundesbank has generally said that discussion of the topic is a political one that should be addressed by European Union finance ministries in the run-up to the currency, slated to begin in 1999.</p>
<p>--Svea Herbst-Bayliss, Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
